Sphere tree by TGlad (Tom Lowe): recursive Eisenstein Ford sphere
packings on a Riemann sphere projection, a dense tree of touching spheres
(fractalforums.org, "New sphere tree", June 2020).

Calculated by mb3d-rs itself (the code above is only a placeholder; the
original Mandelbulb3D shows nothing with this formula).

PackRatio: 0 .. 1.22, the size of the spheres (1: touching).
Levels: how deep the tree goes.
Rotated: 1 turns each level a twelfth of a revolution.
Colour scale: each branch of the tree gets its own colour value (0..1.5,
the orbit trap: "2nd choice" in the Lighting); this scales it.
